ls, and I think I understand how the boundaries impact visibility.\n\n\n**Defining the Rule**\n\nI am now formulating a precise rule for how each pixel influences the final output. The main diagonal of the 2x2 block reveals a very specific equation, where each diagonal is drawn with a color value of 1. It seems like the equation `c - r = 2*(C - R)` dictates where to draw the color within the scaled-up output. I've broken it down step by step, which has greatly clarified my thought process! The diagonal is NOT overwritten!\n\n\n",
